{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the name of the one Eliezer.</b> Even though he is the second-born, it writes about him 'the one,' because his name is called after the first event that happened to him — that on account of it he fled from Egypt — and it seemed to him as though he were the first." "<b>And he delivered me from the sword of Pharaoh.</b> For that Pharaoh who sought to kill Moses died, as it is written in that passage: 'for all the men who sought your life are dead.' Another interpretation: for this reason he does not call him first, for it was not part of the matter of the firstborn, as we said above in the section of Shemot — for regarding the firstborn there was no doubt in his hand to do; and when this one was born, which was for the Holy One, blessed be He, it appeared to him that he was the first."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The phrase 'שהיה להקב״ה' is elliptical; rendered hyper-literally as 'which was for the Holy One, blessed be He,' leaving the implied subject (the birth or the child) unspecified as in the Hebrew. The phrase 'לא היה ספק בידו לעשות' is rendered literally; the referent of the pronoun in 'his hand' is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:27.013086128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}